@page "/docs/components/calendar"
@using Blaizio.Docs.Examples.Calendar
<PageTitle>Calendar - Blaizio</PageTitle>

<div class="typeset typeset-docs space-y-10">
    <header class="docs-page-header space-y-2.5">
        <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2">
            <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Calendar</h1>
            <DocBadges Slug="calendar" />
        </div>
        <p>A date grid for picking a single day, several days or a range, bound to plain <code>DateOnly</code> values. The whole grid works from the keyboard: arrow keys move between days, Home and End jump within the week, and Page Up and Page Down change the month, or the year with Shift held. Set a <code>Culture</code> and the grid follows that culture's own calendar, whether Gregorian, Persian or Hijri, along with its month names, digits and first day of the week.</p>
    </header>

    <UsageBlock Example="typeof(CalendarBasicExample)"
                Description="After importing `Blaizio.Ui`, bind a nullable `DateOnly` to `Value`. Bind `ValueFormatted` as well to read the chosen day back as a string in the calendar's own culture." />

    <ExamplesHeading />

    <Demo Title="Basic" Description="Click a day to select it and click it again to clear it. From the keyboard, tab into the grid, move with the arrow keys and pick with Enter or Space. The readout below is the bound `ValueFormatted`, so no separate formatting call is needed." Example="typeof(CalendarBasicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Multiple" Description="Set `Mode` to `Multiple` to toggle any number of days on and off, bound to a list through `Values`. `ValueFormatted` covers single values only, so this example formats each day with `BzCalendar.FormatValue`." Example="typeof(CalendarMultipleExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Range" Description="With `Mode` set to `Range`, the first click sets the start, the second sets the end and a third starts over. The days in between fill in as a band, and each edge is formatted with `BzCalendar.FormatValue`." Example="typeof(CalendarRangeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Formatting the value" Description="Call `BzCalendar.FormatValue(date, culture)` to format a date in another culture or a range edge. It uses that culture's calendar, month names and digits just as the grid does, so `fa-IR` gives the Persian year 1405 rather than 2026. Plain `DateOnly.ToString` is shown for contrast: it stays on the Gregorian calendar." Example="typeof(CalendarFormattingExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Month & year dropdowns" Description="`CaptionLayout` replaces the caption label with dropdowns, so you can jump straight to a distant month or year. Choose `Dropdown` for both, `DropdownMonths` or `DropdownYears`. The year list covers roughly a century back through ten years ahead by default." Example="typeof(CalendarDropdownExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom year range" Description="Set `FromYear` and `ToYear` to limit the year dropdown to your own span, here a date-of-birth picker that reaches back to 1925." Example="typeof(CalendarYearRangeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Multiple months" Description="`NumberOfMonths` shows several months side by side, and the navigation buttons page through all of them together." Example="typeof(CalendarMonthsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Bounds" Description="`Min` and `Max` limit the selectable window. Days outside it are grayed out, and navigation stops at the first and last allowed months." Example="typeof(CalendarBoundsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled days" Description="Pass a `DisabledSelector` to gray out and block individual days, here every weekend, while the rest stay selectable." Example="typeof(CalendarDisabledDaysExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Hide outside days" Description="Set `ShowOutsideDays` to `false` to hide the grayed days from the neighboring months, which leaves the first and last weeks ragged." Example="typeof(CalendarOutsideExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Date picker" Description="Place the calendar inside a popover to build a date-picker field. The button shows the chosen date, and the popover closes as soon as a day is picked." Example="typeof(CalendarPickerExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Localization" Description="Pass a `Culture` and the month names, weekday names and first day of the week follow it. With German (`de-DE`), the week starts on Monday, and the bound `ValueFormatted` follows the same culture." Example="typeof(CalendarLocalizationExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arabic (Gregorian)" Description="Not every Arabic locale uses the Hijri calendar. `ar-AE` keeps the Gregorian calendar while showing Arabic month and weekday names and Arabic-Indic digits, laid out right to left." Example="typeof(CalendarArabicGregExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Arabic (Hijri)" Description="A culture with a non-Gregorian calendar lays out its own months and years. This `ar-SA` culture carries the Umm al-Qura (Hijri) calendar, set in the code because the calendar a bare `ar-SA` starts in depends on the platform (Gregorian on a Linux server with recent culture data). The grid mirrors inside a right-to-left `DirectionProvider`, and `ValueFormatted` gives the Hijri year 1448." Example="typeof(CalendarArabicExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Latin digits" Description="Numbers default to the culture's native digits (Arabic ١٢٣, Persian ۱۲۳). Set `NativeDigits` to `false` to keep Latin numerals while the calendar, month and weekday names stay localized. `ValueFormatted` follows the same setting, so the readout matches." Example="typeof(CalendarLatinDigitsExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Persian / Farsi (Jalali)" Description="Farsi (`fa-IR`) uses the Persian (Jalali) calendar, with its own months such as Farvardin and Ordibehesht and the year 1405 instead of 2026. The bound value is still an ordinary `DateOnly`, so only the display changes." Example="typeof(CalendarPersianExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Week numbers" Description="`ShowWeekNumber` adds a leading column with each row's week of the year, counted by the culture's week rule." Example="typeof(CalendarWeekNumberExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Custom cell size" Description="Override `--cell-size` for bigger cells and supply `DayContent` to put something under each day. This booking-style example shows a nightly price that rises on weekends." Example="typeof(CalendarCellSizeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Booked dates" Description="Mark taken days with `DisabledSelector`, then style the disabled day through `Class`. Here a strike-through makes booked days easy to spot." Example="typeof(CalendarBookedExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Presets" Description="Quick-pick buttons next to the calendar inside the popover turn it into a date picker with presets." Example="typeof(CalendarPresetExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Date and time" Description="Pair the calendar with an inline `BzInputTime` for a date-and-time picker. The two bind separately, so combine the date and time when you read the value." Example="typeof(CalendarDateTimeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Date and time range" Description="Two time pickers alongside the calendar give a start and end time for a booking slot. Each one binds its own `TimeOnly`." Example="typeof(CalendarDateTimeRangeExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Disabled" Description="`Disabled` grays out the whole calendar and blocks selection and navigation, while the current value stays visible." Example="typeof(CalendarDisabledExample)" />

    <Demo Title="Customization"
          Description="Every part accepts `Class`. This example targets the `calendar-day-button` slot in its `data-selected-single` state to swap the primary fill for indigo, with a matching indigo tint on hover."
          Example="typeof(CalendarCustomizationExample)" />

</div>

